{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1141019-is-there-any-indication-that-minotaur-was-an-apis","id":1141019,"title":"Is there any indication that Minotaur was an Apis?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-17T04:49:14-07:00","id":1141019,"title":"Is there any indication that Minotaur was an Apis?","content":"Was Minotaur an Apis that somehow fell? What do we know of him, and could be connected to that group of Apis known as Last Hope (I think)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T04:57:40-07:00","id":1141021,"title":"","content":"according to werewolf yes he was an apis. on the other hand toreador swear he was a child of their antedilluvian whose beast consumed him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T05:05:05-07:00","id":1141024,"title":"","content":"Hmm... It he is an Apis that disembodied or something then I wonder if he has any of his old Gifts he could use on the Garou's behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:18:11-07:00","id":1141039,"title":"","content":"Need to be careful here: there's Minotaur the mythical figure, who was an Apis, and there's Minotaur the Skin Dancer totem, who's never been given a direct tie to the Apis. We know the mythical Minotaur was responsible for the Minotaur myths, and therefore the form the Skin Dancer totem takes, but no other connection's ever been suggested.<br /> <br /> The totem could maybe be a fallen Apis, but his associations don't seem particularly Apis-like - the man that becomes the beast, the sentient that seeks animalistic power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:36:56-07:00","id":1141739,"title":"","content":"The man that becomes the beast could describe just about any homid Fera with Rage who lets themselves fall into bitterness and hate. But yeah, a small, boxed subsection in a book somewhere or something would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:51:18-07:00","id":1141768,"title":"","content":"I just view it this way: like any mythological figure, the Minotaur myth is based on nearly a half-dozen supernaturals of various sorts, whose stories became blended over time, into a composite story.<br /> <br /> One 'Minotaur' was a beastie Thallain changeling.<br /> One 'Minotaur' was probably a Rank 6 Apis wereaurochs.<br /> One 'Minotaur' was a Gangrel vampire living in Ancient Greece.<br /> One 'Minotaur' was the Skin Dancer tribal totem Middle Umbral spirit.<br /> And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-19-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T12:21:42-07:00","id":1141841,"title":"","content":"The classic Minotaur of legend takes place in Bronze Age Crete several generations before the Trojan War. This roughly places it at around 1400 BC give or take a few centuries. The War of Rage should have taken place several thousand years before this. So the Apis should have been extinct by the time of the legend.<br /> <br /> I think in Changing Breeds for W20, it states that the legendary minotaur was one of the Last Hope who returned from the Umbra thousands of years after they had left Earth, and frenzied in despair that his old family was long gone. So that fits the differences in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}